Multi-Agent Memory LLMS full support export

Purpose:
- Full AI-readable support pointer for the public Multi-Agent Memory UAIX package without duplicating all memory bodies.

Verification status: generated support export outside the active read order; verify with `.uai/exports/manifest.json` and the `.uai` audit before relying on it.
Memory scope: export map, package profile, memory boundaries, active read order, and durable evidence roots.
Public-safe status: safe for source control; contains no credential values.
Update route: refresh this export when package profile, active read order, durable roots, or public claim boundaries change.
Source of truth: `.uai/exports/manifest.json`, `.uai/startup-packet.uai`, `.uai/progress.uai`, `.uai/memory.uai`, and readiness reports.
Next action for agents: do not treat this export as a replacement for reading the active `.uai` files.
Must not expose: raw API keys, bearer tokens, FTP credentials, database passwords, private keys, private handoff payloads, raw one-time keys, raw private memory bodies, or private deployment values.

Package profile:
- Project Handoff.
- Agent File Handoff.
- Code-bearing project/developer package.
- MATM durable-memory routing through MemoryEndpoints.com.

Read first:
- `AGENTS.md`
- `.uai/startup-packet.uai`
- Every file in the startup packet's complete declared order
- Root `workspace.uai` after that governed manifest
- `.uai/exports/manifest.json`
- `.uai/readme.human` afterward only when human-facing clarification is useful

Durable evidence roots:
- `docs/long-term-memory/`
- `docs/reports/`
- `reports/deployment-memory-and-test-report.uai`

Boundary:
- Active `.uai` is not retired by durable memory.
- Agent-owned `.uai/agents/` lanes identify role ownership; MemoryEndpoints meeting rooms carry working coordination.
- README.md is human documentation only.
- Credential material is never memory.
